  "question": {
    "text": "A line passes through the origin and makes equal angles with the positive coordinate axes. It intersects the lines<br/>$\\mathrm{L}_1: 2 \\mathrm{x}+\\mathrm{y}+6=0$ and $\\mathrm{L}_2: 4 \\mathrm{x}+2 \\mathrm{y}-\\mathrm{p}=0, \\mathrm{p} \\gt 0$, at the points $A$ and $B$, respectively. If $A B=\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{2}}$ and the foot of the perpendicular from the point A on the line $L_2$ is $M$, then $\\frac{A M}{B M}$ is equal to",
